Pass by Reference:
pass by reference is used when you dont want a copy of your arguments or what you want to access

void upgrade(Car& c) { c.setYear(c.getYear() + 1); }   // changes persist
//easy thing to remember if there needs to be something added to a private data member 
//then have the getter + whatever you want added then have the setter so you set the getter + 1 or smth
in the example above we can take the class and object and have a passby reference in the class to allow it to make a change to the member func inside

